INT. MARINE AQUARIUM - SHARK TUNNEL - NIGHT

Blue gloom. Silhouettes of rays drift overhead. Reflected ripples slide across black-clad figures crouched along the tunnel wall.

VESPER LOWRY (30s, crew boss, earpiece) taps a panel. MUNGO TAKAHASHI (40s, safe man, fingers like a surgeon's) kneels at a locked case. "PIPS" ADEBAYO (20s, tech, tablet glowing on her forearm). ROSALIND CHEN-MARCH (50s, driver, quiet), watches the corridor. DUKE ZELENSKY (30s, muscle, nervous) checks his watch.

                    VESPER
          Eyes up. Ninety seconds on the loop.

                    PIPS
          Cameras show tank two. No movement.

                    DUKE
          (muttering)
          Tank two. Sure. Tank two.

                    MUNGO
          Quiet. I'm in.

A latch clicks. He lifts out a velvet tray. Pearls the size of marbles, gleaming.

                    VESPER
          Rosalind, status.

                    ROSALIND
          Clear.

Footsteps echo. Everyone freezes. A shadow lengthens along the curved glass.

ILSE VANTERPOOL (60s, security guard, cardigan under her uniform, thermos in hand) rounds the corner. She sees the crew. Sees the pearls. Sips her tea.

                    ILSE
          I don't get paid enough for this.

                    VESPER
          Nobody does. Everybody, stay calm.

                    ILSE
          Is there a plan for me?

                    PIPS
          (to Vesper, low)
          She's not on the schedule.

                    VESPER
          (to Ilse)
          There's a plan. You sit. We leave. You call it in in five minutes, with a good story.

                    ILSE
          I have a bad knee.

                    DUKE
          Just sit!

She sits. On the floor. Shark shadows pass over her face.
